{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals","id":1199098,"title":"Most Useful Blood Sorcery Rituals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-24T10:02:26-07:00","id":1199098,"title":"Most Useful Blood Sorcery Rituals","content":"We all have our favorites, our &quot;go to&quot; ritual. What are your favorite blood sorcery rituals of levels 1-5? Specifically, why is it so amazing? Is it V20 or classic?<br /> <br /> My current favorite is Craft Wierding Stone (Koldunic Sorcery ritual, level 2 from Caine's Chosen - The Black Hand): Like the Bloodstone ritual the caster always knows distance and heading to the location of the stone. The stone can also allow the user to send a telepathic message to the caster, and also allows the wielder to know the direction to go to find what they seek. Give one of those to your ghouls when you send them out to smoke a rival; they can update you on the fly, and even if the target is moving you will find him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:11:43-07:00","id":1199101,"title":"","content":"Apport Object, most recently reprinted in Red List. It's Thaumaturgy 1 and it allows you to enchant an object to teleport to you on command. Aside from keeping your Thaumaturgy 5 talisman safe from being stolen, it also allows you to steal things (provided you have 5 minutes to enchant them), do sick magic tricks at parties, bring any tool you might want to you when you need it, smuggle things into any area, and other fun and useful things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>g3taso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals#post1199098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current favorite is Craft Wierding Stone (Koldunic Sorcery ritual, level 2 from Caine's Chosen - The Black Hand): Like the Bloodstone ritual the caster always knows distance and heading to the location of the stone. The stone can also allow the user to send a telepathic message to the caster, and also allows the wielder to know the direction to go to find what they seek. Give one of those to your ghouls when you send them out to smoke a rival; they can update you on the fly, and even if the target is moving you will find him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I have one of those! It's called a &quot;smartphone&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:34:05-07:00","id":1199109,"title":"","content":"Of the usual (core book) ones<ul><li>Illuminate the Trail of Prey - that very parctical if you need to find or follow someone</li> <li>Burning Blade - Weapon with Agg damage</li> <li>Donning the Mask of Shadows - that almost like getting Obfuscate for free (at least in the V20 version)</li> <li>Principal Focus of Vitae Infusion - beeing able to store and carry around lots of blood is also very practical</li> <li>Pavis of Foul Presence - be completely save from Presence and even throw the effects back on the one who tried to used them on you</li> <li>Enchant Talisman - the DAV20 version lets you (if I understand it correctly) cast Rituals up to level 4 without the usual (quite long) casting time, which eliminates the main downside of rituals in comparison to discipline powers</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:47:54-07:00","id":1199113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1199101#post1199101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apport Object, most recently reprinted in Red List. It's Thaumaturgy 1 and it allows you to enchant an object to teleport to you on command.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know on what page, I can't find it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T11:00:33-07:00","id":1199118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1199113#post1199113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know on what page, I can't find it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was wrong, it's not actually in Red List. You can find it in Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat p.51.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T11:23:00-07:00","id":1199124,"title":"","content":"-The various Ward and Warding Circle rituals are all useful. Being able to keep ghouls away from certain things is, alone, invaluable in the Jyhad. As are Wards against ghosts, if you manage to run afoul of a necromancer, or are Haunted (like with the Flaw).<br /> <br /> -Defense of the Sacred Haven is a literal unlife-saver, by turning any area into an impromptu haven, safe from sunlight.<br /> <br /> -Domino of Life can be useful for social-focused blood sorcerers, or even just blood sorcerers who have low Humanity and can't employ the blush of life easily. If you absolutely need to pass as human, this ritual is a cheap way of proving your credentials as a living person. Might help a vampire dodge suspicion from vampire hunters.<br /> <br /> -Recure of the Homeland heals aggravated damage faster and more cheaply than doing it just with blood. If a sorcerer gets into a lot of fights, and they either unlive in their home city or have a bunch of its soil on hand, it can expedite the healing process, at least a little.<br /> <br /> -Clinging of the Insect can be very useful for getting around. For just the price of a live spider, the sorcerer turns any surface into navigable terrain. Need to escape but all land passages blocked? Scale the walls. Need to hide in a room with no cover? Few people ever bother to check the ceiling. Want to set up an emergency or supplementary haven that can't be accessed easily? Have the entrance be on the side of a sheer cliff, or up some shaft with no stairs, etc. It's worth noting that while other Discipline powers could replicate these advantages, they aren't native to many blood sorcerers (like, for instance, the Tremere).<br /> <br /> -Speaking of rituals to enhance mobility, Incorporeal Passage makes physical barriers a non-issue. Walk through walls, slip out of manacles. So long as the sorcerer has access to a mirror shard, they can escape from most mundane traps and bypass most mundane barriers. And the duration of this effect is measured in <i>hours</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T12:02:55-07:00","id":1199139,"title":"","content":"Suspension of Incantation (4) is extremely useful. You can prepare traps, displays of power and other neat tricks. The more paths you know the more versatile it gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T13:41:35-07:00","id":1199169,"title":"","content":"Oh Like this topic! I'll get back once I find the names of the two rituals I'm thinking of!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:36:55-07:00","id":1199196,"title":"","content":"Also quite good:<ul><li>Sanctify the Temple (Rites of Blood,Old Skool Sorcery) - Level 1 Ritual that decreases all difficulties for Pathpowers and Rituals in it by -1 for a Month, very usefull</li> <li>Ambrus Kelemen\u2019s Aegis (V20 Dark Age) \u2013 gives you some Bonus dice you can use for a soak roll or to detect an ambush, nice little buff</li> <li>Blood into Water (Rites of Blood) - Level 1 let spilled Blood Vanish, helps keeping the masqurade</li> <li>Illusion of Peaceful Death (Rites of Blood) \u2013 Level 2 make it look like someone died naturally, dito</li> <li>Beacon of the Self (New York by Night) \u2013 level 3 find the location of an other vampire, handy for detective stories</li> <li>Consecration of the Sanctum (Players Guide to the Low Clans) - level 4 similar to Sanctify the Temple but it effects only rituals, not as good as &quot;Sanctify the Temple&quot; but it is Tremere Thaumaturgy</li> <li>Preservation of the Sanguine Heart (Rites of Blood) \u2013 level 4 immunity against Bloodbonds for a few days</li> <li>Vires acquirit eundo (Bloodmagic) - Level 5 increases the duration of an other Ritual, makes other Rituals even better</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:38:34-07:00","id":1199198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1199118#post1199118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wrong, it's not actually in Red List. You can find it in Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat p.51.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah OK, there is also a level 3 ritual named &quot;<span style=\"font-size:10px\">Translocation of the Vessel</span>&quot; in Rites of Blood that does something similar.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T09:45:21-07:00","id":1199399,"title":"","content":"There's this Tremere NPC I had who had loaaaaaaaaads of &quot;useless&quot; rituels that are, actually, great for what he does : rituals to grow back hairs, domino of life, pavis of foul presence, all the bureaucratic rituals, the rituals to make people pretty or keep shiny art works safe or clean your herd of its diseases.<br /> <br /> Why is it so useful? Because he lives in Paris, France, a Toreador focused city, and with enough selling skills you can definitly sell those rituals as services to the Ventrue and Toreador living there. Most of those rituals are so cheap it's worth doing them for trivial boons. He's managed to become every Toreador's best friend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:55:06-07:00","id":1199516,"title":"","content":"For it's level; Extinguish is a great ritual. It helps against one of the banes of Vampires. Putting out fires with a word (If prepared earlier)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:05:58-07:00","id":1199520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1199516#post1199516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For it's level; Extinguish is a great ritual. It helps against one of the banes of Vampires. Putting out fires with a word (If prepared earlier)</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavily depends on the version. The best one is <i>Ashes of Agni's Curse</i>, which lets you enchant a handful of ashes that then last forever and can be used on demand. <i>Extinguish Flames</i> in Red List p.101 is hilariously useless - it's a level two ritual with no pre-cast, so I hope you have spare ten minutes to cast it while the fire consumes you. <i>Extinguish</i> in DAV20 p.304 is okay, with caveats. You pre-cast it at the start of the night, so it's a nightly drain on your blood resources if you are sufficiently paranoid to get good use out of it. It also requires pinching a candle, which provokes Rotschreck and could result in aggravated damage. The ritual specifically doesn't say that, but you are a highly flammable vampire and some other magic rituals deal aggravated damage in similar circumstances so an ST might call for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 03-26-2018, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T09:21:16-07:00","id":1200459,"title":"","content":"Pavis of Foul Presence is a great way to make your ST hate you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:32:22-07:00","id":1201385,"title":"","content":"Firewalker is invaluable if you're a member of the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:02:07-07:00","id":1201404,"title":"","content":"- Bans are great and underrated. And they are a great plot device! A nightclub that was shut down because Baali were using it to summon up an Earthbound, running a cult in the club. The Tremere put up a Ban once the infernalists were dead, for Infernal Powers like Lores. But Bans are broken when violence occurs inside the Ban...<br /> <br /> So when the Anarch PCs in my game torch the chantry and kill most of the Cammies in the city, no one is maintaining the Ban. And when a guy kills his wife and hangs himself in one of the apartments in the building (which was converted from a club after being closed)... well now we have a powerful Earthbound in the building itself, free to do as it pleases, waking up from a long nap.<br /> <br /> They also make a neat Elysium ritual. No one can use Disciplines inside the ban, meaning that Elysium is more of a neutral space. An interesting option.<br /> <br /> - Kolduns have a ritual where they can use a bowl of water to restore Willpower. Just, immediately. Once a night, but still very useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T17:29:49-07:00","id":1201480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1201404#post1201404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Bans are great and underrated. And they are a great plot device! A nightclub that was shut down because Baali were using it to summon up an Earthbound, running a cult in the club. The Tremere put up a Ban once the infernalists were dead, for Infernal Powers like Lores. But Bans are broken when violence occurs inside the Ban...<br /> <br /> So when the Anarch PCs in my game torch the chantry and kill most of the Cammies in the city, no one is maintaining the Ban. And when a guy kills his wife and hangs himself in one of the apartments in the building (which was converted from a club after being closed)... well now we have a powerful Earthbound in the building itself, free to do as it pleases, waking up from a long nap.<br /> <br /> They also make a neat Elysium ritual. No one can use Disciplines inside the ban, meaning that Elysium is more of a neutral space. An interesting option.<br /> <br /> - Kolduns have a ritual where they can use a bowl of water to restore Willpower. Just, immediately. Once a night, but still very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you have a reference for the Bans and in particular how they can negate a Lore? I find it hard to interesting that Thaumaturgy Ritual can trump an Earthbound's power and want to take a gander at the RAW and see if it's something I might use/allow in my current chronicle or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23951-acwrig2","name":"acwrig2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T04:17:48-07:00","id":1201583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acwrig2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1201480#post1201480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you have a reference for the Bans and in particular how they can negate a Lore? I find it hard to interesting that Thaumaturgy Ritual can trump an Earthbound's power and want to take a gander at the RAW and see if it's something I might use/allow in my current chronicle or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the Dark Ages 20 books, Bans are listed. I think it might be the Book of Secrets or something?<br /> <br /> So you can have a Ban that stops Fae stuff, or Demon stuff, or Shifter stuff, or Vampire stuff, or Wraith stuff. But ALL Bans break the moment there is violence inside them.<br /> <br /> The logic here is that Bans are powerful but situational. Most Tremere don't know how to Ban demonic powers, and mostly don't need to, and when they do it costs a lot of blood and takes up time. This was a special case where the Prince called in favours to preserve the Masquerade, and the Chantry was devoted to keeping this Ban up until they were torched.<br /> <br /> Now I wouldn't let a PC thaumaturge create a Ban which simply Stops Demon Powers up to the level of an Earthbound. This is a plot device for an NPC. However a PC could, with the Ban rituals, create a space where regular Demons were next to powerless. But they can leave, or do something violent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T07:20:36-07:00","id":1201607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acwrig2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1201480#post1201480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you have a reference for the Bans and in particular how they can negate a Lore? I find it hard to interesting that Thaumaturgy Ritual can trump an Earthbound's power and want to take a gander at the RAW and see if it's something I might use/allow in my current chronicle or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bans are listed in the Tremere Apocrypha section of the V20 Dark Ages Companion, p. 116. Violence committed in a Banned space is not mentioned, from what I'm reading, save perhaps for Discipline/magic use (which in itself might violate the Ban) that may or may not be violent in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T19:59:50-07:00","id":1201828,"title":"","content":"Many of my favorites were already listed here, but here's some I didn't see mentioned from my Elder Tremere's character sheet:<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Contract</b>(Thaumaturgy 5): In a world where people lie and deceive constantly, being able to create a contract that forces people to keep to the word is immensely valuable, both in your own dealings and as a broker of such a service.<br /> <b>Court of Hallowed Truth</b>(Thaumaturgy 5): This ritual is priceless. Enchants an entire room, duration is measured in weeks, and &quot;No falsehood may be spoken, and direct questions from the presiding judge or power are answered candidly with <b>no omissions or deceit.&quot; </b>That's right folks, this ritual literally prevents people from lying by omission to you, or by misleading you with things that are technically true. Pure, solid gold.<br /> <b>Sanctuary</b>(Thaumaturgy 5): Requires a willpower point, but lasts a year and prevents any <i>souls</i>(not just people) from entering the building without the casters explicit permission. All inside are protected from Auspex, Dominate, Dementation, and other mental/emotional disciplines. Violence breaks it, but pretty much makes the structure invulnerable to any kind of subterfuge.<br /> <b>Stone of the True Form</b>(Thaumaturgy 5): Precast, engage in a willpower contest to force things to assume their &quot;natural&quot; form. Explicitly includes Obfuscated creatures, shapeshifters, and fleshcrafting.<br /> <b>Bone of Lies</b>(Thaumaturgy 4): Detects lies. It's okay.<br /> <b>Invisible Binding Chains</b>(Thaumaturgy 4): Explicitly casts instantly with no weird components, creating some pretty strong bindings that has a scaling number of targets. Anyone with potence will break them easily, anyone without is going to have a rather tough time.<br /> <b>Scry</b>(Thaumaturgy 4): Keep an eye on your enemies. Probably your friends, too. People shed dead skin/hair everywhere they go, so a smart Tremere with Auspex can even identify someone who's only passed through an area.<br /> <b>Mirror of Second Sight</b>(Thaumaturgy 3): I love rituals that make permanent items. This ritual makes a small item that lets you see all supernatural creatures in their true forms. Easily identifies every kind of supernatural, and reveals anyone hiding with superpowers.<br /> <b>Ascension of the Blood</b>(Thaumaturgy 2): Removes blood bonds from vitae. Since vampires need to ingest blood to learn disciplines, use certain abilities, or maybe can only feed on it if they have that one flaw, this is immensely useful.<br /> <b>Blood Walk</b>(Thaumaturgy 2): Each success allows you see up one generation from your victim, giving you the &quot;true name&quot; and face of all their ancestors, as well as identifying the subjects generation and clan. Even assuming that &quot;true name&quot; isn't of the magically potent variant, this is amazing for a 2nd level ritual because you'll never run into a situation where you capture an enemy and can't identify their sire. Three successes also reveals all vampires the target shares a blood bond which either way, which is even more awesome.<br /> <b>Craft Bloodstone</b>(Thaumaturgy 2): Lets you make up to WP rocks that you have full positional awareness of. I know GPS exists in modern nights, but this is much more secure.<br /> <b>Machine Blitz</b>(Thaumaturgy 2): Depends on whether or not your ST determines &quot;takes effect instantly&quot; to mean this ritual does not have a casting time. If it is instant, this ritual is very good, allowing you to put a stop to car chases, computers, and guns with ease. If not, it's kinda useless. Taking 10 minutes to break machines is something you could usually do with a hammer.<br /> <b>Seal Egress</b>(Thaumaturgy 2): Creates a perfect seal for a room, with a duration measured in decades. Does not physically reinforce it, but prevents any and all kinds of non-natural mystical entry. Very powerful defense for a second level ritual.<br /> <b>Chime of Unseen Spirits</b>(Thaumaturgy 1): If you got problem with ghosts, this is a decent ritual. If your ST buys that you can wear the chime as an earring or necklace, it's good for not getting spooked.<br /> <b>Learning the Mind Enslumbered</b>(Thaumaturgy 1): If only the victim could tell us what they saw in their last moments! No problem.<br /> <b>Sangenious Phial</b>(Thaumaturgy 1): Stores blood. Not as good as principal focus, but is level 1.<br /> <b>Wake With Evening's Freshness</b>(Thaumaturgy 1): Immediately awakens you from sleep at any sign of danger and lets you ignore daytime penalties for a few rounds while you massacre whoever is sneaking into your haven. I'd rather have it and not need it then need it and not have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","user":"Zanos","date":". 03-31-2018, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:23:28-07:00","id":1202829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1201607#post1201607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Bans are listed in the Tremere Apocrypha section of the V20 Dark Ages Companion, p. 116. Violence committed in a Banned space is not mentioned, from what I'm reading, save perhaps for Discipline/magic use (which in itself might violate the Ban) that may or may not be violent in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Will have to check that out. I've never played in Dark Ages. It's always just been lore/history for the modern nights games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23951-acwrig2","name":"acwrig2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T11:39:31-07:00","id":1480755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1199098-most-useful-blood-sorcery-rituals?p=1200459#post1200459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pavis of Foul Presence is a great way to make your ST hate you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which in turn is a great way to have your character destroyed, lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}